A||||4||JBananas||Question on axle repair costs||||5||
Z||000000||JBananas||02-15-2000||07:13 PM||||I found a way to bend my axle. How much would it cost to replace say through a mechanic and if I so choose to do myself how hard and long would it take to repair?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||02-15-2000||07:54 PM||||If you bent an axle you may very well have done other damage also. Be sure to get everything else in your suspension checked. As for replacing an axle it is not overly difficult and a replacement should be about $100US<p>[This message has been edited by Phil (edited 02-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||02-15-2000||10:51 PM||||I replaced both axels in my 85 SE v-6 4spd when I replaced the engine.  I got remanufactured axels for $69.00 each from Ken's auto in Pelham, AL.  I believe Autozone was about the same price.<P>They aren't hard to replace.<P>How did you bend yours?||||reg||1
Z||000003||ggarsk||02-16-2000||02:41 AM||||They aren't that had to replace...of course I can say that now that I've finished mine. They should cost anywhere from 60 to 100 dollars,it depends on where you get them. Shop around find the best price. In the technical section there is a topic on drive axle replacement. Check it out,it will help...it helped me alot. and if you can swing it I'd change both of them. Good luck||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||02-16-2000||12:49 PM||||I don't even want to know how...... Those axles are very sheltered. very likely you have other problems as well. ||||reg||1
